      "content": "That makes sense, but I'm looking for more specifics based on the demographic maps I have. Specifically, I've noticed that in a lot of these cities, areas with high levels of ethnic diversity or rapid changes in the racial makeup tend to see more flux in property values. From an investment standpoint, how do you factor racial or ethnic composition shifts into your \"stability\" assessment? Does a more homogeneous demographic profile generally signal a safer, more predictable investment compared to an area that's becoming more diverse?",
